# Patterns

Reference implementations: `src/PlayUp/web/src/design-lab/` (visual arbiter).

## Overview (Vue d'ensemble)

Composition emerges from lifecycle state, top to bottom:
1. Hero band (≈1.6/1): "Où en est-on ?" (hero numeric + one-sentence reading
   + cycle line) | "Prochaine action" (eyebrow + title + why + primary button).
2. À traiter groupe (only if items exist): D9 rows.
3. Sport band (≈1.45/1): current matchday | compact standings.

## Prochaine action

Always exactly one, always with a "why" line, always the only primary button
of the surface.

## Match Hero (fiche match)

Object header with three states — center swaps, frame stays:
- Scheduled: kickoff time as hero numeric, "Démarrer le match" primary.
- Live: score hero + minute badge, +/− stepper under each team,
  "Terminer le match" primary.
- Finished: score hero, "Résultat officiel" pill, ghost "Corriger le résultat".
Meta band below: calendar/clock/pin icons + referee, on surface-secondary.

## Calendrier

One panel; rounds as typographic sections (label + date + state pill);
MatchRow per match; live rows outrank everything.

## Classement

Legend before table; zones as left bars; Pts dominant; trends slanted.

## Accueil

Hub ops hors Shell: lockup + one panel of interactive rows (crest, name,
declared dates, status, chevron). Hover A: `--color-surface-secondary`
full-bleed wash; chevron → ink. Pressed = hover. No brand bar, shadow, lift,
or underline. Whole row is one hit target. Lockup proportions (mark vs
wordmark + tagline) are the same at desktop / tablet / phone: the block
scales as a unit when the 42rem column is narrower. Phone: padding and
safe-area tighten; Créer stacks under the section title.

## Empty / loading / error

- Empty states explain **what will appear and why** ("Les matchs apparaîtront
  ici dès que…"), optional single secondary action. Never an illustration dump.
- Loading: quiet text/status placeholders, no shimmer.
- Error: `error` tone, reserved for real failures — never for pending work.
